  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Remove the \"message\" listener on unmount instead of only nulling the socket",
      "body": "After `mount(socket)` and `unmount()`, the anonymous listener registered at line 14 is never removed — `unmount()` only sets `this.socket = undefined`, and the closure reference was lost by inlining it. On any socket that outlives the view, subsequent `\"message\"` events still call `this.render(message)` on the unmounted view (stale renders). Because the closure captures `this`, the socket also retains the `SocketView` indefinitely, preventing garbage collection. Repeated mount/unmount cycles on the same socket accumulate listeners, causing duplicate renders and unbounded listener growth. The removed code stored `this.onMessage` precisely so `off(\"message\", this.onMessage)` could deregister it; restore the stored handler (or otherwise keep a reference) and detach it in `unmount()`.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/socket-view.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 14,
        "end": 18
      }
    }
  ],
